 seems to understand the  danger of an economy relying on foreign  products is mr futterman the same guy  who has a richard nixon campaign poster  hanging in his house a decade after  nixon's resignation as president of the  united states  [Music]  we seek friendly relations with all  nations any nation can be our friend  without being any other nation's enemy i  have taken this action because of my  profound conviction that all nations  will gain from a reduction of tensions  and a better relationship between the  united states and the people's republic  of china richard nixon's relations with  china are well recognized as one of the  most meaningful parts of his presidency  now i'm no more an expert on politics  than i am on dog breeds but from what i  understand nixon was instrumental in  opening up more trade between the us and  china in his book seize the moment he  wrote if we want to have an impact on  the changes occurring in china we should  not pull the plug on trade his goal was  for american companies to have a  presence in china but what actually  happened was american companies began  producing goods in chinese factories to  save money but perhaps mr futterman  initially supported nixon because of his  intention to take advantage of free  trade with china but now he's grown  tired of seeing made in china all over  everything he buys  [Music]  united is still shipping him over here  they put them in the cars they put them  in the tv they put them in the stereos  and the radios just stick in your ears  and put them on your watches they got  little teeny gremlins  as billy walks kate home that evening  she even hints that the only reason for  his rage against foreign products may be  related to the relocation of jobs  overseas he's been like that ever since  he lost his job  he's like a lot of people around here it  seems like a lot of citizens are  blissfully unaware of the problem like  the deputy at the police station when  billy comes to warn him that